WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.441
was bent over a tubular device when Zann and his friends walked in.

2
00:00:16.461 --> 00:00:18.202
"You're alive!"

3
00:00:18.642 --> 00:00:20.243
she cried, rushing over to hug them.

4
00:00:20.263 --> 00:00:23.504
"When I got back here and you were gone, I feared the worst!"

5
00:00:23.524 --> 00:00:26.305
"Sorry," Perda said sheepishly.

6
00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:27.946
"We should've left you a note."

7
00:00:28.766 --> 00:00:30.347
Fala stepped back and glared at them.

8
00:00:31.427 --> 00:00:33.472
"Yes, you should have," she scolded.

9
00:00:33.492 --> 00:00:36.633
"Never mind— I'm just glad you're okay.

10
00:00:36.953 --> 00:00:38.133
But we have a problem."

11
00:00:38.153 --> 00:00:40.354
"You're right," Zann said.

12
00:00:40.374 --> 00:00:42.135
"We were just at the palace."

13
00:00:42.155 --> 00:00:44.135
"What's going on at the palace?"

14
00:00:44.555 --> 00:00:45.175
asked Fala.

15
00:00:45.876 --> 00:00:48.096
Zann and the others told Fala what had happened.

16
00:00:49.116 --> 00:00:52.737
Fala nodded when they got to the part about Morb appearing in the throne room.

17
00:00:53.538 --> 00:00:56.778
"One of my contacts at the palace was supposed to check in an hour ago.

18
00:00:57.579 --> 00:01:00.319
When I didn't hear from him, I used the Remote Eye."

19
00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:02.240
She gestured at the device.

20
00:01:04.296 --> 00:01:06.678
"I saw Morb walking around in the throne room.

21
00:01:07.419 --> 00:01:10.521
But the Eye doesn't have sound, so I couldn't hear what he was saying."

22
00:01:10.541 --> 00:01:12.243
"Did you see Yog?"

23
00:01:12.563 --> 00:01:13.144
Zann asked.

24
00:01:14.145 --> 00:01:15.506
"No," Fala replied.

25
00:01:15.526 --> 00:01:16.807
"I hope he's safe.

26
00:01:17.187 --> 00:01:19.249
And I'm glad you kids got out when you did."

27
00:01:19.269 --> 00:01:22.091
"We almost didn't," Gliss told her.

28
00:01:22.111 --> 00:01:24.293
"We ran into a troll on our way out."

29
00:01:24.313 --> 00:01:27.816
"Well, Zann did, anyway," Perda added.

30
00:01:28.557 --> 00:01:30.579
That reminded Zann of the silver talisman.

31
00:01:30.959 --> 00:01:32.120
He described it to Fala.

32
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:37.324
"Do you think Morb could be using talismans to send extra power to the trolls?"

33
00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:38.144
he asked.

34
00:01:38.165 --> 00:01:41.707
"That sounds like something I've seen in the ancient texts."

35
00:01:42.148 --> 00:01:43.189
Fala looked intrigued.

36
00:01:43.209 --> 00:01:49.654
"Such talismans wouldn't only provide extra power— they could also be a way for Morb to control the

37
00:01:49.694 --> 00:01:54.258
trolls. If only we could get our hands on one of those talismans.

38
00:01:55.078 --> 00:01:56.459
It could be invaluable to us."

39
00:01:56.479 --> 00:02:02.428
"Yeah, well, good luck finding someone crazy enough to go up to a troll and take it," said

40
00:02:02.468 --> 00:02:05.430
Perda. "So what should we do now?"

41
00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:06.811
Zann asked Fala.

42
00:02:07.571 --> 00:02:09.392
"We freed a lot of Reds earlier.

43
00:02:10.253 --> 00:02:13.614
If we all work together, maybe we can stop Morb."

44
00:02:14.395 --> 00:02:15.295
Fala looked worried.

45
00:02:15.656 --> 00:02:18.317
"Most of those Reds aren't ready to face Morb yet.

46
00:02:18.977 --> 00:02:21.519
They're staying hidden, not using magic.

47
00:02:22.259 --> 00:02:24.661
Venna and her people are trying to devise a plan."

48
00:02:25.001 --> 00:02:25.521
She shrugged.

49
00:02:25.541 --> 00:02:30.324
"Maybe you kids should head home—you'll be safer there until we figure out what to do.

50
00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:32.285
Do you have a way to get there?"

51
00:02:32.305 --> 00:02:35.286
"We rode here on dragons," Darb said.

52
00:02:35.306 --> 00:02:37.107
"We left them grazing in the forest."

53
00:02:37.867 --> 00:02:41.809
"We're not going home—I don't have a home to go to," Zann said.

54
00:02:41.829 --> 00:02:45.790
"My grandfather was taken and so were Gliss' parents."

55
00:02:46.671 --> 00:02:47.311
Gliss nodded.

56
00:02:47.331 --> 00:02:50.352
"Swamp Bottom isn't any safer than First City.

57
00:02:50.652 --> 00:02:51.713
We're staying here."

58
00:02:51.733 --> 00:02:53.994
"All right," said Fala.

59
00:02:54.014 --> 00:02:56.435
"But it's getting late—let's get some sleep.

60
00:02:57.155 --> 00:02:59.016
Tomorrow could be a very long day."

61
00:03:00.724 --> 00:03:03.985
Late that night Morb stood alone in the palace courtyard.

62
00:03:04.705 --> 00:03:08.686
Sweat poured off his forehead as he focused every bit of energy he could gather.

63
00:03:08.706 --> 00:03:12.247
"Come to me," he murmured.

64
00:03:12.967 --> 00:03:14.748
His entire body shook with effort.

65
00:03:15.388 --> 00:03:19.189
With the magic he'd taken from all those Reds, was he strong enough to do this?

66
00:03:20.509 --> 00:03:21.730
His energy began to waver.

67
00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:23.950
Sharp pains were shooting through him.

68
00:03:24.611 --> 00:03:28.112
But he'd waited too long for this moment—he wouldn't wait any longer.

69
00:03:28.492 --> 00:03:29.472
It had to be now!

70
00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:33.982
Morb's knees buckled as he focused every ounce of energy on his task.

71
00:03:34.842 --> 00:03:38.124
Falling to the ground, he writhed back and forth in agony.

72
00:03:38.464 --> 00:03:39.524
And that was all it took.

73
00:03:40.945 --> 00:03:42.786
The extra bit of friction shot through him.

74
00:03:42.806 --> 00:03:47.948
"Yes!" he gasped as he felt his energy shift.

75
00:03:48.948 --> 00:03:51.910
Crash! His eyes popped open and he smiled.

76
00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:57.392
His masterpiece, the new machine, stood before him in all its evil glory.

77
00:03:58.184 --> 00:04:04.910
Its enormous frame of wire and bone gleamed in the starlight, and the paralyzer pythons writhed angrily in

78
00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:05.870
their glass prison.

79
00:04:06.651 --> 00:04:10.974
Morb climbed to his feet, still shaking from the effort of moving the machine all the way from

80
00:04:10.994 --> 00:04:11.555
the fortress.

81
00:04:12.556 --> 00:04:14.717
For a moment he considered summoning Wyssa.

82
00:04:15.418 --> 00:04:20.942
He only needed a few more items, starting with the Skellian sea sponge she'd promised to bring him

83
00:04:21.002 --> 00:04:25.966
tomorrow. If he ordered her to fetch it now, the machine would be complete that much sooner.

84
00:04:26.687 --> 00:04:27.688
But he decided to wait.

85
00:04:28.112 --> 00:04:30.233
After all, what was one more day?

86
00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:36.474
Very soon now, he would have everything he'd ever dreamed of back in his pathetic Void days.

87
00:04:37.615 --> 00:04:41.196
When Zann awoke the next morning, his friends were eating puckerberry pancakes.

88
00:04:41.976 --> 00:04:43.956
Zing was slurping dragon mush nearby.

89
00:04:43.976 --> 00:04:47.537
"We didn't want to wake you," Perda said when Zann sat up.

90
00:04:47.557 --> 00:04:50.318
"We figured you needed the extra sleep."

91
00:04:51.098 --> 00:04:51.818
Darb grinned.

92
00:04:51.838 --> 00:04:54.399
"Plus Perda wanted to eat all your pancakes."

93
00:04:55.539 --> 00:04:56.560
Zann hurried over to them.

94
00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:57.780
"Where's Fala?"

95
00:04:58.004 --> 00:04:59.365
he asked, grabbing some food.

96
00:04:59.385 --> 00:05:02.607
"She was gone when we woke up," Gliss said.

97
00:05:02.627 --> 00:05:06.430
"She left a note telling us to stay here until she gets back."

98
00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:08.291
Zann didn't say anything.

99
00:05:08.671 --> 00:05:11.133
He finished his breakfast and then headed toward the door.

100
00:05:11.153 --> 00:05:12.894
"Where are you going?"

101
00:05:13.254 --> 00:05:13.835
Perda asked.

102
00:05:13.855 --> 00:05:17.757
"I want to see what's going on outside," Zann replied.

103
00:05:18.478 --> 00:05:22.640
When he turned the doorknob, it started spinning so fast that he couldn't hold onto it.

104
00:05:23.361 --> 00:05:25.863
Then a little toy bird popped into view.

105
00:05:25.883 --> 00:05:29.337
"Nice try, kids," it said in Fala's voice.

106
00:05:30.017 --> 00:05:32.178
The others laughed, but Zann frowned.

107
00:05:33.578 --> 00:05:36.199
He thought about trying to find a way to breach Fala's spell.

108
00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.201
But without using magic, it seemed hopeless.

109
00:05:39.921 --> 00:05:44.323
He realized he had no choice but to stay there as she'd asked—at least for a little while.

110
00:05:45.103 --> 00:05:46.864
Luckily he didn't have to wait too long.

111
00:05:47.644 --> 00:05:49.385
Fala burst in 15 minutes later.

112
00:05:49.405 --> 00:05:50.845
"What's wrong?"

113
00:05:51.245 --> 00:05:53.546
Zann asked when he saw the grim look on her face.

114
00:05:53.566 --> 00:05:57.148
"I've been out gathering the latest news," Fala replied.

115
00:05:57.905 --> 00:05:59.230
"It's not good."
